 "pair": "ru-en",
 "title": "Настоящий профессионал  (A True Professional)",
 "level": "A1 — Duolingo Section 2",
 "labels": {
  "barinov": "Шеф",
  "max": "Макс"
 },
 "segments": [
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": "Max has been given a kitchen jacket and is eager to show off. Chef Barinov first sends everybody back to work, and then turns to Max with some pointed questions about what a professional cook actually does. This is the conversation in Russian first.",
   "gap": 0.8
  },
  {
   "v": "barinov",
   "t": "Все за работу, быстро!",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "barinov",
   "t": "А ты иди переодевайся!",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "max",
   "t": "Шеф, я готов. Что мне делать?",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "barinov",
   "t": "Почему ты пришёл на эту кухню?",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "max",
   "t": "Потому что я повар. Я настоящий профессионал.",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "barinov",
   "t": "Профессионал? Иди сюда.",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "barinov",
   "t": "Посмотри вокруг на моих поваров.",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "barinov",
   "t": "Что ты сам умеешь делать?",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "max",
   "t": "Я очень хорошо умею готовить.",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "barinov",
   "t": "Да ну? Всем внимание на кухне!",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "barinov",
   "t": "К нам пришёл великий повар!",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "barinov",
   "t": "Мы так долго ждали его!",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "max",
   "t": "Какая у меня будет работа?",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "barinov",
   "t": "Для тебя есть особенная работа!",
   "gap": 0.9
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": "Let's go back over the chef's questions.",
   "gap": 0.4
  },
  {
   "v": "barinov",
   "t": "Все за работу, быстро!",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": "'Everyone get to work, quickly!' No verb at all: Barinov just says \"everyone onto work\", and ",
   "gap": 0.25
  },
  {
   "v": "barinov",
   "t": "за работу",
   "gap": 0.25
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": " with -u is how you send people to a task. ",
   "gap": 0.25
  },
  {
   "v": "barinov",
   "t": "Быстро",
   "gap": 0.25
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": ", quickly, is the word behind the word for faster.",
   "gap": 0.4
  },
  {
   "v": "barinov",
   "t": "А ты иди переодевайся!",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": "'And you, go get changed!' ",
   "gap": 0.25
  },
  {
   "v": "barinov",
   "t": "А ты",
   "gap": 0.25
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": " is \"and you\", with ",
   "gap": 0.25
  },
  {
   "v": "barinov",
   "t": "а",
   "gap": 0.25
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": " for contrast: everyone else works, you change. ",
   "gap": 0.25
  },
  {
   "v": "barinov",
   "t": "Переодевайся",
   "gap": 0.25
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": " is ",
   "gap": 0.25
  },
  {
   "v": "barinov",
   "t": "пере-",
   "gap": 0.25
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": ", re-, plus the verb to dress, and the final \"-sya\" means you're dressing yourself.",
   "gap": 0.4
  },
  {
   "v": "max",
   "t": "Шеф, я готов. Что мне делать?",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": "'Chef, I am ready. What should I do?' ",
   "gap": 0.25
  },
  {
   "v": "max",
   "t": "Готов",
   "gap": 0.25
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": " is \"ready\", from the same family as the verb to cook: cooking is getting things ready. ",
   "gap": 0.25
  },
  {
   "v": "max",
   "t": "Что мне делать",
   "gap": 0.25
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": " is \"what to me to do\".",
   "gap": 0.4
  },
  {
   "v": "barinov",
   "t": "Почему ты пришёл на эту кухню?",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": "'Why did you come to this kitchen?' The chef says ",
   "gap": 0.25
  },
  {
   "v": "barinov",
   "t": "ты",
   "gap": 0.25
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": " to his new cook straight away. ",
   "gap": 0.25
  },
  {
   "v": "barinov",
   "t": "На эту кухню",
   "gap": 0.25
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": " ends in -u because it's movement toward a place; being in the kitchen would use a different ending.",
   "gap": 0.4
  },
  {
   "v": "max",
   "t": "Потому что я повар. Я настоящий профессионал.",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": "'Because I am a cook. I am a true professional.' ",
   "gap": 0.25
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": "The word for why asks and ",
   "gap": 0.25
  },
  {
   "v": "max",
   "t": "Потому что",
   "gap": 0.25
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": " answers: they are a matching pair. ",
   "gap": 0.25
  },
  {
   "v": "max",
   "t": "Профессионал",
   "gap": 0.25
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": " is borrowed.",
   "gap": 0.4
  },
  {
   "v": "barinov",
   "t": "Посмотри вокруг на моих поваров.",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": "'Look around at my cooks.' ",
   "gap": 0.25
  },
  {
   "v": "barinov",
   "t": "Вокруг",
   "gap": 0.25
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": " is ",
   "gap": 0.25
  },
  {
   "v": "barinov",
   "t": "в",
   "gap": 0.25
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": " plus ",
   "gap": 0.25
  },
  {
   "v": "barinov",
   "t": "круг",
   "gap": 0.25
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": ", in a circle, so \"around\". ",
   "gap": 0.25
  },
  {
   "v": "barinov",
   "t": "Посмотри",
   "gap": 0.25
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": " is \"look\". ",
   "gap": 0.25
  },
  {
   "v": "barinov",
   "t": "Моих поваров",
   "gap": 0.25
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": " is \"my cooks\", ending in the plural \"-ov\".",
   "gap": 0.4
  },
  {
   "v": "barinov",
   "t": "Что ты сам умеешь делать?",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": "'What can you do yourself?' ",
   "gap": 0.25
  },
  {
   "v": "barinov",
   "t": "Сам",
   "gap": 0.25
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": " is \"yourself\", which pushes the question back at Max. ",
   "gap": 0.25
  },
  {
   "v": "barinov",
   "t": "Умеешь",
   "gap": 0.25
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": " is \"you know how to\", the skill word.",
   "gap": 0.4
  },
  {
   "v": "max",
   "t": "Я очень хорошо умею готовить.",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": "'I can cook very well.' ",
   "gap": 0.25
  },
  {
   "v": "max",
   "t": "Хорошо",
   "gap": 0.25
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": " is \"well\", from the word for good. ",
   "gap": 0.25
  },
  {
   "v": "max",
   "t": "Умею готовить",
   "gap": 0.25
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": " is \"I know how to cook\", with Max sure of himself.",
   "gap": 0.4
  },
  {
   "v": "barinov",
   "t": "Да ну? Всем внимание на кухне!",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": "'Really? Attention everyone in the kitchen!' ",
   "gap": 0.25
  },
  {
   "v": "barinov",
   "t": "Да ну",
   "gap": 0.25
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": " is a sarcastic \"really?\". ",
   "gap": 0.25
  },
  {
   "v": "barinov",
   "t": "Всем внимание",
   "gap": 0.25
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": " is \"to everyone, attention\", with ",
   "gap": 0.25
  },
  {
   "v": "barinov",
   "t": "всем",
   "gap": 0.25
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": " the \"to\" form of \"all\".",
   "gap": 0.4
  },
  {
   "v": "barinov",
   "t": "К нам пришёл великий повар!",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": "'A great cook has come to us!' ",
   "gap": 0.25
  },
  {
   "v": "barinov",
   "t": "Великий",
   "gap": 0.25
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": " is \"great\", as in a great king, and here it's mockery. ",
   "gap": 0.25
  },
  {
   "v": "barinov",
   "t": "К нам",
   "gap": 0.25
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": " is \"to us\".",
   "gap": 0.4
  },
  {
   "v": "barinov",
   "t": "Мы так долго ждали его!",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": "'We waited for him for so long!' The -li on ",
   "gap": 0.25
  },
  {
   "v": "barinov",
   "t": "ждали",
   "gap": 0.25
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": " is the plural past ending, so \"we waited\". ",
   "gap": 0.25
  },
  {
   "v": "barinov",
   "t": "Его",
   "gap": 0.25
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": ", him, is the same word as \"his\", and in that \"his\" sense it never changes.",
   "gap": 0.4
  },
  {
   "v": "max",
   "t": "Какая у меня будет работа?",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": "'What work will I have?' ",
   "gap": 0.25
  },
  {
   "v": "max",
   "t": "У меня будет",
   "gap": 0.25
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": " is \"at me will be\", the \"I have\" pattern in the future. ",
   "gap": 0.25
  },
  {
   "v": "max",
   "t": "Какая",
   "gap": 0.25
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": ", \"what kind of\", ends in \"-aya\" to match ",
   "gap": 0.25
  },
  {
   "v": "max",
   "t": "работа",
   "gap": 0.25
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": ".",
   "gap": 0.4
  },
  {
   "v": "barinov",
   "t": "Для тебя есть особенная работа!",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": "'There is a special job for you!' ",
   "gap": 0.25
  },
  {
   "v": "barinov",
   "t": "Есть",
   "gap": 0.25
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": " is \"there is\", a word Russian often leaves out in the present, so when the chef says it, he means it. ",
   "gap": 0.25
  },
  {
   "v": "barinov",
   "t": "Для тебя",
   "gap": 0.25
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": " is \"for you\", in the friendly form. Now let's listen to the whole conversation again from start to finish.",
   "gap": 0.9
  },
  {
